<title>UK: GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nick Price jumps three places to</p>
<p>ninth spot in the world rankings issued on Monday.</p>
<p>Price earned his return to the top 10 with an eight-stroke</p>
<p>victory in the Data Dimension Pro-Am at the weekend.</p>
<p>At the top, Greg Norman maintains his clear lead over Tom</p>
<p>Lehman while Mark O'Meara overtakes Britain's Colin Montgomerie</p>
<p>in third place.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>  1. Greg Norman (Australia)     11.70 points average</p>
<p>  2. Tom Lehman			 9.69</p>
<p>  3. Mark O'Meara		     9.00</p>
<p>  4. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)  8.95</p>
<p>  5. Ernie Els (South Africa)     8.74</p>
<p>  6. Nick Faldo (Britain)	   7.98</p>
<p>  7. Fred Couples		     7.77</p>
<p>  8. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	  7.58</p>
<p>  9. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	  6.87</p>
<p> 10. Davis Love III		   6.85</p>
<p> 11. Corey Pavin			6.80</p>
<p> 12. Phil Mickelson		   6.45</p>
<p> 13. Steve Stricker		   5.88</p>
<p> 14. Tiger Woods			5.82</p>
<p> 15. Scott Hoch			 5.79</p>
<p> 16. Steve Elkington (Australia)  5.70</p>
<p> 17. Bernhard Langer (Germany)    5.49</p>
<p> 18. David Duval			5.37</p>
<p> 19. Steve Jones			5.37</p>
<p> 20. Mark McNulty (Zimbabwe)	5.32</p>
</text>
